                                "sense_id": "42fdbfbf-47a2-3138-ab88-85f2cf8268d8",
                                "text": "That Castle was most goodly edifyde, / And plaste for pleasure nigh that forrest syde […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "012f748f-b55e-3b8a-82ba-c7d4c11083b5",
                        "entry_id": "a9ce17a0-7ced-3964-b564-52e7c9c24520",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To instruct or improve morally or intellectually."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad9b1424-e3b5-4737-858f-475f63d1922a",
                                "sense_id": "012f748f-b55e-3b8a-82ba-c7d4c11083b5",
                                "text": "January 23, 1783, Edward Gibbon, letter to Dr. Priestley\nIt does not appear probable that our dispute [about miracles] would either edify or enlighten the public."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "deba6ba6-69c0-4066-bf6e-499200483c93",
                                "sense_id": "012f748f-b55e-3b8a-82ba-c7d4c11083b5",
                                "text": "That they ought to edify one another by maintaining and promoting the knowledge of truth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a249301-36c8-465c-a2a6-1f052e6c8a1d",
                                "sense_id": "012f748f-b55e-3b8a-82ba-c7d4c11083b5",
                                "text": "frustrate the best endeavours in the edifying of the church"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
